            <ArticleTitle>Co-incidental diagnosis of an extradural abscess while siting an extradural catheter for postoperative analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>845-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extradural abscess is a rare but serious complication of the extradural route of administration of analgesic drugs. We report a case of spontaneous extradural abscess diagnosed during placement of an extradural catheter for analgesia after a negative diagnostic laparotomy. Magnetic resonance imaging is the usual diagnostic tool of choice. This, and subsequent surgery, confirmed the diagnosis suspected after drainage of pus through the Tuohy needle.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
